<!--
  SoLID-Lite stage-2 (SIDIS-lite) solenoid field for the PROVISIONAL magnet compact/magnet/solenoid_lite_sidis.xml:
  CLEO-II iron + front piece, 5 upstream shields, donut and 2 bottom plates of the 2026-09-30 workshop model (no plug,
  no nose, no correction coil). 2D axisymmetric (r-z) map solenoid_SoLIDlite_stage2_2D, solved with magnet_field/
  (rzfield finite elements, open boundary, POISSON's 1010-steel table) on magnet_field/models/solid_lite_stage2.am,
  the r-z model extracted from this geometry (CLEO-II coil 1282 turns x 3266 A). This is NOT the later CLEOv11 design
  of "CLEO-II Stage 1 and 2.html" (plug, -16.2 kA-turn correction coil, nose, bridge, 3 back plates; Bz(0,-350 cm)
  tuned to 0.02 G in POISSON's box, 13 G with an open boundary): replace the magnet and this map together when that
  design is built. Reference values (map): Bz(0,0) = 13463 G, Bz(0,-315 cm) = 69.4 G, Bz(0,-350 cm) = 19.8 G,
  |B|(r 215, z 344 cm) = 101.8 G, integral Bz dz on axis 5.259 T m (z -600..800 cm).
  File: GEMC ASCII map with <mfield> header (R 0..500 cm x Z -600..800 cm, 1 cm, gauss, cylindrical-z; 30.4 MB);
  grid and unit are read from the header and cross-checked against <dimensions>. scale is dimensionless (e.g. -1 to
  flip the polarity; scaling the current this way ignores saturation).
  The map is looked up in ./fieldmaps, then in ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps, else downloaded there once from the
  fieldmaps-v1 release of solid_dd4hep; its sha256 is checked, and an earlier download of another version is
  replaced. Offline: copy the release file into ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps/. To regenerate it from a checkout
  (python3 with numpy, scipy and gmsh; about 2 min; magnet_field/README.md):
      magnet_field/make_maps.sh -n -f ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps stage2
  (-n solves the committed deck after checking that the checkout's magnet files are those it was extracted
  from; without -n the deck is first re-extracted from the DD4hep geometry in the eic_xl container). A regenerated
  map has its own header comment (how and when it was made), so its sha256 differs from the release file's: to
  use it, set sha256 to the value the checksum error reports.
-->
<lccdd>
  <fields>
    <field type="SoLID_FieldMapB" name="SolenoidField" field_type="magnetic" coord_type="BrBz"
           field_map="fieldmaps/solenoid_SoLIDlite_stage2_2D.dat"
           cache="${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps"
           url="https://github.com/JeffersonLab/solid_dd4hep/releases/download/fieldmaps-v1/solenoid_SoLIDlite_stage2_2D.dat"
           sha256="9ea03a8711b1e91e5fbda46499a10b77a3fce07c3e24335cb2c9c7c4e007432b"
           hint="Generate it from a solid_dd4hep checkout: magnet_field/make_maps.sh -n -f ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps stage2 (magnet_field/README.md)"
           scale="1.0">
      <dimensions>
        <R step="1.0*cm" min="0*cm"    max="500*cm"/>
        <Z step="1.0*cm" min="-600*cm" max="800*cm"/>
        <translationCoord x="0*cm" y="0*cm" z="0*cm"/>
      </dimensions>
    </field>
  </fields>
</lccdd>
